WEBVTT

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.990
Maki!

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.090
Stop!

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.740
Walton!

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.190
Wait!

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:39.610
What is it, Walton?

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:40.800
Is something there?

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.620
You did it, Walton!

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.750
You found one!

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.020
A fairy!

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.220
A big, big fairy!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.200
So do it for her, if not for yourself...

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.780
<i>Don't make me repeat myself!
So do it for her, if not for yourself...</i>

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:39.190
But...

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.240
Thirteen's not a little kid anymore.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.610
That's what I want.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.180
What the gentleman's trying to say...

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.350
...is that she should be with young people her own age.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.540
Grandpa, I found a giant fairy on Silver Lake!

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.550
This wouldn't be...

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:01.800
Go play outside.

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:05.210
Come on.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.530
Well, she's getting to be a little lady.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.310
Y-You crazy coot!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.400
O-Old man...

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.710
You forget who you're dealing with!

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:37.680
That piece of tin won't do any good when you're dead.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.030
Don't bother us again.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:01.880
Damn geezer.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.330
Who is that old man anyway?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.530
A killer.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.380
Decorated in the last war.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.890
How about a picnic?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.000
The girl? But...

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.710
The geezer's not here, so don't worry.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.210
But still...

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:30.380
Want HQ to think you're weak?

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.680
Well...

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.040
Then it's decided.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.500
Morgue's a good name for this place.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.080
Don't you think?

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.250
Gravity's twisted around here.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.410
There must be lingering radiation.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.850
Alien motors?

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:13.980
The giant alien robot seems to have made a full recovery.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.160
Bigfoot.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:24.160
"Giant Alien Robot EX-1" is too much for one breath.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.610
Special explosion.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:36.670
They burn whatever's in their path.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.950
Which battalion fought here?

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:42.210
Troop 223.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.680
So they bought this with their subsidies.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.650
Captain.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.900
Their final report.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.620
17 dead.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:55.130
And just one survivor.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:58.700
He's recovering at the Garfield Military Hospital.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.100
Something wrong, sir?

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.820
How many do you see?

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:05.790
Well, 17...

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:08.940
Where's the man that dropped this?

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.810
Dan, how much longer do you need?

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.080
Almost finished.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.450
Good.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.240
Let's go find Bigfoot.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:33.100
Hello, there...

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.070
...Harriet.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.840
How would you like to come with us and make some new friends?

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.070
It'll be more fun than staying with your grandpa.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:48.380
She don't talk to no one but her dog and grandpa.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.480
Look here.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.450
Come with us.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:54.850
Walton!

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.390
Are you all right?

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.830
Yeah, it's not bad.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.800
The question is if you're fit to walk up those mountains.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.570
The picnic's over.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:07.730
Let's go hunting.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.730
This is where the army's radar lost it, 0521.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.310
No record after that.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.180
It likely went by ground.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.780
If the satellite's working, we could order a composite scan.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.550
Headquarters calling.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.520
Put it through.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.590
Give me your report.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:37.130
We're at the last contact point. About to explore the surface.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.060
The army has the instruments,

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:43.200
but not the personnel to go after such a large target.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.000
It's us or nobody.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.340
In the end, we're doing their dirty work.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:48.270
Lt. Harris.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.880
Did you check the data I sent?

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.480
I'm going down to the hospital.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.180
He was part of the main staff at the lab.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.450
He can probably tell us a lot.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.490
Please do.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:02.290
Call in if you find anything.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:10.160
As you heard, this is our chance to show what we can do.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:11.960
Any sign of metal or movement?

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:12.930
No, sir.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:14.870
Any gravity noise?

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.640
Nothing detected.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.400
There's nothing but pine trees.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.940
It can't move far without showing itself.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:22.540
Target that patch there.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.750
Roger, I'll scan the area and put it on a 3D map.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:28.610
Unless it's in a hole in the ground,

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.080
we should be able to see it.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:31.950
What is it?

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:33.190
Just one thing.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.450
It seems he doesn't want to be found.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.590
Hey!

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.940
Mr. Fairy!

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:50.470
I made you a present!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.330
Come out wherever you are!

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:22.100
These dolls you make are so strange.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.400
That's because they're fairies.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:27.740
No way, fairies are cuter.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.010
The ones with wings?

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.140
There are those too.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.990
I've seen these fairies.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:41.090
In the deserts of the Middle East, in the corners of Asia.

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:44.210
I've seen fairies in all kinds of places.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.650
Were they good fairies?

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.030
Yes, they were good fairies.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:58.330
They were all my friends.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.440
Can people become fairies?

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:03.780
Of course.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.480
They can become fairies,

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.650
and go to a far, faraway land.

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:09.820
Neverland?

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.280
Or to Oz?

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.270
A land much further away.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:17.590
That's where your mom and dad are.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:40.410
You...

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:41.910
...saved me?

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:50.360
Can't we rest a little?

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.520
Real hunters don't rest till they bag their prey.

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:04.720
There, it's a perfect fit!

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.640
I'm giving it to you.

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.010
In return,

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:13.260
could you do something for me?

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.900
I thought you'd be here.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.300
We've been looking for you.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:23.590
So, will you come with us...

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:24.990
...Hattie?

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.520
Well, come here.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.990
You'll get to go to school.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:33.370
You'll make lots of friends.

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.420
And do a lot of fun things.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:57.660
No!

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:02.530
You...

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.230
Relax.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:09.030
I only shot the sky.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.800
But...

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:13.400
Heard the noise and dropped like a baby.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:16.010
You mean...

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.880
You never heard that before?

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.870
It's like hunting grizzlies, fire in the air and they drop.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.470
Come on, stand up.

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:36.830
Shut up, damn mutt!

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.100
Don't!

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.150
Move it!

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:50.670
Walton!

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:53.080
Run! Hurry!

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.140
You'll get shot!

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:06.990
I have it on map.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.730
It's the EX-1.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:12.860
48°, 55 minutes north latitude. Longitude of 110° and 15.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:13.830
Good.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.330
Don't lose it.

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:39.190
Hattie.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:44.430
Hurry!

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.160
Go lower. I can't get a reading.

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:16.260
There's no way.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:17.920
The specs say you can.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.000
They're not flying this thing.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.470
Can we use the SARG?

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:25.370
We can, but the spoilers aren't adjusted,

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:27.940
and it's not tested for high altitudes.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.000
There'll be another accident.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.810
I'll go.

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:35.560
The SARG tested fine at short distances.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.720
And I had the top training score.

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.720
Please give me the order.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.390
I can back him up with these systems.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:45.340
At least on the scanners.

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:48.010
All right, go.

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:06.410
Don't push it above 18% capacity.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:07.310
Any more...

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:08.280
I know.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:12.480
Any more and the cockpit's
inertial eliminators could freeze.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:13.740
Right.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.290
It'll be fine.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.750
If it looks dangerous, I'll come right back.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:19.310
SARG 1, stand by.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.800
Standing by.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.140
You've got a 20 minute limit.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:34.070
Roger!

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.970
SARG 1, all clear.

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:38.410
Eject!

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:50.120
Dan!

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.820
No need to worry!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.540
Where's my granddaughter?

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:08.730
I-I don't know.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.640
There's a monster here!

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:12.770
We've gotta run!

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:15.410
Grandpa!

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:16.610
Hattie!

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:18.210
I found a fairy!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.400
He brought a friend with him!

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.260
Alien jammers locked on!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.000
It's a different one from the EX-1.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.430
And the EX-1?

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.940
It's not moving.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.270
Any civilians?

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.200
I'm checking.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.080
Mama!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:30.750
No!

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.490
Get away from here!

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:44.900
Papa!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.770
Over here!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.540
Mr. Fairy.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.590
You came back for me?

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:33.800
Please...

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:37.860
Take me with you.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:46.150
To that far, faraway place where everyone's waiting.

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:57.960
Headquarters, I've spotted the EX-1.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.090
Now moving in.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.700
There's been a fire.

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:04.430
Request local emergency units to search...

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:12.340
SARG 1, awaiting transmission.

00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:15.180
Please respond, SARG 1.

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>They all went away to a great, distant land.</i>

00:22:26.890 --> 00:22:34.530
<i>Where together they play...</i>

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:54.490
<i>Where springs become summers and green meadows lie.</i>

00:22:54.490 --> 00:23:00.890
<i>And the babbling brooks babble, and the dragonflies fly.</i>

00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:05.700
That's an old song.

00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:10.400
Don't we have a class together?

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:15.270
Sorry, you don't remember, huh?

00:23:17.710 --> 00:23:19.080
I'm Takuto.

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:22.080
Takuto Kaneshiro, a Space Engineering major.

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:25.600
Me too.

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:33.120
What's that?

00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:34.250
I couldn't hear.

00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:53.900
Maki.

00:23:55.480 --> 00:23:57.070
I couldn't hear you...

00:23:58.120 --> 00:23:59.120
...Maki.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:09.790
Two souls, attracted to each other...

00:24:09.790 --> 00:24:13.060
Innocence and grace, so beautiful,

00:24:13.060 --> 00:24:15.700
and so very dangerous.

00:24:15.700 --> 00:24:18.640
Next time,
The Maiden and the Meeting.
